From 1dfa978b7a6d39d599743026d3a8bd1a18f72f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:03:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: EXLR8 dense trellis as stored (q_b, o_proj, layers 0-2
 MLP, shared expert pieces): E4M3 EXL3 linear for decode rows, exact bf16
 rebuild for prompt GEMMs (patch 0205b)

kindlingai's EXLR8 (exlr8-v2) trellis matrices were rounded to bf16 by the converter (X8 interim) and then packed to q8
at load. They now load as stored: EXL3 tiles marked mcg_e4m3, cut to the rank by whole 128-blocks. Decode rows run
TensorFold's exl3_linear on a new image built with TF_EXL3_MCG_E4M3=1 (exl3_linear_e4m3); prompt chunks rebuild the
matrix as bf16 rows (kernels/cuda/exlr8_recon.cu: integer transforms, f64 scales, one rounding) for the tiled bf16 GEMM.
Only a config with codebook mcg_e4m3 probes for the markers or loads the new modules; every existing image is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
